    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1040">

                <pb facs="0646" n="1696" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p2/pg1696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.919/7–2153: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in India</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Allen</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of
                        State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1040-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-07-21T16:00:00+05:30">July 21, 1953—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>147. Pursuant request from Naval Attaché for investigation, Polish vessel SS <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mickiewicz</hi>, Bombay ConGen reports consignment by GOI-owned Indian Rare Earths Limited to Taku Bar, China of 2,248 pounds
                    “foreign” thorium nitrate valued rupees 40,500. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mickiewicz</hi> departed Bombay July 17 for Colombo. Embassy requested
                    urgent clarification facts shipment from GOI and
                    will cable results.</p>
                <p>Bombay requested clarify word “foreign” and provide Department and Embassy with
                    any additional information available on subject.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Allen</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1040-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1040-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was also repeated to Bombay as telegram 39.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
